# PhotosAI — Code Style Guide

Follow these conventions in all new code. Full guide: `docs/CODE_STYLE.md`

## Structure
- One component per file in `src/components/`
- Extract reusable logic into `src/hooks/`
- Shared constants in `src/constants.js`
- Keep `App.jsx` thin (~100 lines) — orchestration only

## React
- Functional components; no class components
- `useCallback` for handlers passed as props
- `useRef` for DOM (canvas, input); avoid refs in dependency arrays unless linter requires
- Prefer composition over prop drilling

## Naming
- Components: PascalCase (`EditorSidebar.jsx`)
- Hooks: camelCase with `use` prefix (`useEditHistory.js`)
- Constants: UPPER_SNAKE (`INITIAL_EDIT_STATE`, `FILTER_PRESETS`)

## Styling
- Tailwind only; no CSS modules or styled-components
- Use semantic classes: `text-zinc-400`, `bg-zinc-900`, `accent-indigo-500`
- Responsive: `lg:` for sidebar layout changes

## File Organization
```
src/
├── components/   # UI components
├── hooks/        # Custom hooks
├── constants.js  # Shared config
└── utils/        # Pure helpers (when added)
```

## When Adding Features
1. Add constants to `constants.js` if reusable
2. Create component in `components/` and export from `index.js`
3. Update `docs/PROGRESS.md` and `docs/ROADMAP.md` after committing
